<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imperial Asiatic Company of Trieste</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1775–1785</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Imperial Asiatic Company of Trieste and Antwerp</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Imperial Asiatic Company of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trieste">Trieste</a> was an Austrian trading company founded in 1775 on the initiative of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-bolts">William Bolts</a>, a former servant of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>. Sailing under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> flag, it set up posts at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delagoa-bay">Delagoa Bay</a> in south-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicobar-islands">Nicobar Islands</a> and traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Over-expansion and debt led to its bankruptcy in 1785.</p></div>
